ytail, a silver forehead ornament with a red gem at its center, and dark-blue armored robes with red trim and silver shoulder guards.\n<Subject 3> is the rainy urban street environment in <Picture 3>, featuring a corner convenience store at night, neon signs in Korean and Chinese, wet asphalt reflecting colorful lights, passing cars, and heavy rainfall.\n<Audio 1> is the voice-timbre reference for <Subject 1> (S1), a soft female vocal layer.\n<Audio 2> is the voice-timbre reference for <Subject 2> (S2), a male vocal layer.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation + audio reference] The target video depicts a 10-second emotional reunion on a rainy night city street between <Subject 1> and <Subject 2>, two xianxia characters who meet again after many years in the modern urban setting of <Subject 3>. She exits the convenience store, they spot each other across the street, time slows as they walk toward one another, and he speaks her name in quiet disbelief. <Audio 1> and <Audio 2> provide the voice timbres for the two characters.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3], [Shot 4]): partially_preserved - her facial features, black double-bun hairstyle with pearl ornaments, and white flowing silhouette are retained, adapted into a modern long white coat that echoes her hanfu's elegance while fitting the urban rainy-night context.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3], [Shot 4]): partially_preserved - his facial features, long black ponytail, and dark imposing silhouette are retained, reimagined as a dark tailored long coat with subtle silver details that echo his original armor's aesthetic.\n<Subject 3> (appears in all shots): fully_preserved - the rainy night intersection, corner convenience store, neon signage, wet reflective asphalt, traffic, and atmospheric lighting are fully retained as the complete setting.\n<Audio 1>: reference - its soft female vocal timbre and emotional quality guide <Subject 1>'s whispered line and breath sounds without copying the original signal.\n<Audio 2>: reference - its male vocal timbre and delivery guide <Subject 2>'s spoken line and emotional intonation without copying the original signal.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video uses a cinematic romantic-drama style with moody neon lighting, cool blue tones contrasted by warm amber convenience-store glow, visible rain streaks throughout, and slow, deliberate camera movement.\n[Shot 1] A wide shot of <Subject 3>, the rainy urban intersection at night. The corner convenience store glows warmly, its glass shelves visible through rain-streaked windows. Neon signs in red, green, and blue reflect vividly on the wet asphalt. A car drives through a puddle in the background. The automatic glass door of the convenience store slides open, and <Subject 1>, the woman with black double buns and a flowing white coat, steps out holding a small paper bag and a transparent umbrella. She pauses on the sidewalk, adjusting her umbrella. Across the street, <Subject 2>, the man with long black hair tied back and a dark long coat, stands at the crosswalk waiting for the light, rain dripping off his hood. The camera slowly pans between them, building anticipation.\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.500, the shot cuts to a medium shot of <Subject 2> from the front. He lifts his head and looks across the street, and his eyes widen — he has spotted <Subject 1>. The rain continues to fall around him, and the red traffic light casts a crimson glow on his face. His lips part slightly in disbelief. The camera slowly pushes in on his face, the background neon blurring into soft bokeh.\n[Shot 3] At 00:04.500, the shot cuts to a medium shot of <Subject 1> from across the street. She feels his gaze and looks up from her umbrella, her eyes locking onto <Subject 2>. Her hand freezes on the umbrella handle. Her expression shifts from confusion to recognition — her eyes glisten, and she draws a quiet, shaky breath using the soft, breathy vocal quality referenced from <Audio 1>. Rain droplets cling to her eyelashes. The traffic light changes, and pedestrians begin to cross between them, momentarily obscuring the view.\n[Shot 4] At 00:06.500, the shot cuts to a side-angle medium two-shot as <Subject 1> and <Subject 2> walk toward each other through the rain, meeting in the middle of the crosswalk in front of the convenience store. They stop a short distance apart, rain falling between them. <Subject 2> (S2) speaks first, his voice low and thick with emotion, using the deep male timbre referenced from <Audio 2>, saying softly, <d>[Chinese] 七月...是你吗？</d> <Subject 1> (S1) looks up at him, her eyes welling with tears, and whispers in the soft vocal quality referenced from <Audio 1>, <d>[Chinese] 孟川...</d> The camera slowly circles around them as they stand face to face, the neon-lit rain continuing to fall around them, and holds on the moment as the video ends.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nConstant heavy rainfall throughout, with water dripping from store awnings and splashing on the wet street. Distant traffic sounds — car engines, tires on wet pavement, and a bus braking nearby. The convenience store's faint interior hum. Rain pattering on umbrella fabric and on coat shoulders. Pedestrian footsteps splashing through puddles during the crosswalk scene.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA gentle, melancholic piano melody at a slow tempo, beginning softly with single notes and gradually adding warm string undertones as the characters recognize each other. The music swells subtly when they speak each other's names, then fades to a held piano chord at the end, leaving the sound of rain as the final lingering layer."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name": "text", "label": "text", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "text"}], "flags": {}, "type": "Text", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#535", "size": [239.94027709960938, 205.51930236816406], "pos": [-1952.5704345703125, 5267.21484375], "id": 142, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {